{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"**ESCALATION — THE DEFECT IS PRE-EXISTING AND WIDER THAN THIS TICKET. `verify`'s `model: standard`, landed by 172e and NOT part of my change, is ALSO ignored.**\n\nThe run finished with NINE per-call records (`REBAR_USAGE_LOG`). EVERY ONE on `anthropic:claude-opus-4-8`, under a config where frontier=`bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8` and standard=`anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6`:\n    1 code-review-base                             opus   (mine: model: frontier)\n    2 code-review-docs                             opus   (batch criterion)\n    3 code-review-tests                            opus   (batch criterion)\n    4 code-review-deletion-impact                  opus   (batch criterion)\n    5 code-review-project-review-phase-boundaries  opus   (batch criterion)\n    6 code-review-api-compat                       opus   (batch criterion)\n    7 code-review-verify                           opus   <-- **172e's `model: standard`, NOT my change**\n    8 code-review-coach                            opus   (mine: model: standard)\n    9 code-novelty                                 opus\n\n`verify` (`code-review.yaml:171`) has declared `model: standard` since story 172e closed. Under this config that MUST resolve to `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6`. It resolved to opus. **That declaration predates my change entirely**, which means the code-review gate has never honoured a per-step model declaration — this is NOT a regression I introduced, and it is not fixable by editing the YAML.\n\nCONSEQUENCES, stated plainly:\n1. **My 3768 change is correct in FORM but INERT**, and so is 172e's. The YAML is right; the runtime ignores it. Gerrit 1169 is +1/+1 but must not be read as delivering the behaviour.\n2. **This ticket's real scope is the PLUMBING, not the declarations.** Its own Problem section says \"Code review is only PARTLY split\" on the strength of `verify` declaring a class — that premise is now falsified: the split does not exist AT ALL at runtime, because no declaration is honoured.\n3. **172e closed with this latent.** Its criterion \"each of the three verifier paths resolves the `standard` class\" was evidently satisfied by unit tests over the resolution helpers rather than by an observed runtime binding — the same gap that let my 9 tests pass. Worth a follow-up ticket rather than a silent fix here; I am not filing one unilaterally.\n4. The `[operator-attested]` criterion CANNOT be satisfied yet, and should not be. The honest reading of this run is that it DISPROVES the behaviour the criterion asks me to demonstrate. Its failure was the gate doing its job.\n\nWHY EVERY CHEAPER PROBE WOULD HAVE MISLED, recorded because the discrimination mattered three times:\n* The caching-warning lines captured only 3 of 9 calls (they fire only when caching was requested and had no effect), so my first extraction under-sampled and I wrongly announced, then retracted, a conclusion drawn from 3/8.\n* A NON-inverted config would have shown `anthropic:claude-opus-4-8` for a working frontier class too — identical to inheritance — so it could not have detected this at all.\n* \"Config not loaded\" was eliminated separately: with the same env var, `load_class_slots()`/`resolve_class('frontier')` returns `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8`, with and without `repo_root=`.\n\nNEXT: find where the code-review gate drops `step['model']` (compare against the plan-review path, which demonstrably DOES honour classes — its 41/1 opus/sonnet split was observed live on eb58), fix the plumbing, then add an end-to-end test that asserts the model each step RECEIVES via a recording runner. Only after that is the live attestation meaningful."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785606439971246001,"uuid":"5aa4858e-f93d-4726-8143-5dffb405248e"}